# Runtime configuration is NOT committed — the whole folder. application.properties and
# logback-spring.xml are placed per environment (local / test / prod) by whoever owns that
# environment, not shipped in the repo.
#
# Leading slash, and it matters. A bare `config/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, so it
# would also swallow src/main/java/com/hodi/config/ — the Java package holding SecurityConfig,
# RedisConfig and CacheConfig. Those would be ignored, never committed, and invisible to
# `git status` (ignored files are not listed), so the repository would not contain a compilable copy
# of the application. Anchoring the pattern keeps this entry's intent — the deployment folder at the
# repository root — without claiming every directory that happens to share its name.
/config/

# Maven
.mvn/timing.properties

# Playwright MCP test artifacts
.playwright-mcp/

# Local file-storage uploads (S3 fallback)
uploads/

# Claude Code local settings (shared settings.json is committed)
.claude/settings.local.json*

# Worktrees created by Claude Code sessions — separate repos, never part of this one.
.claude/worktrees/

# JVM crash / attach artifacts
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
.attach_pid*

# Build & IDE leftovers
out/
HELP.md
.flattened-pom.xml
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
*.orig
*.rej
.fleet/
.zed/
